WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.500
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week’s
episode of Doctor Who totally blew my mind,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.500
not the whole episode.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.630
It’s definitely going to go down as one
of the more fun scary episodes but there was

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.340
just one scene that melted my face off.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.449
So just like normal I’m going to do my top
5 moments, list all the classic references

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.500
I could find and do my review.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.770
Hello to any new people, I do weekly Doctor
Who videos and a weekly giveaway.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:28.519
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:32.090
So important stuff, careful for spoilers from
the episode if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.040
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.040
Top 5 moments.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.200
Number 5 - Clara and Danny’s Date

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.480
It was a nice reversal on that first time
they met, only this time we were seeing it

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.480
unfold from Clara’s perspective.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.329
And we got to see her apartment.

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:51.140
Does anyone else get the sense that Moffat
is trying to see how many funny places he

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.010
can park the TARDIS in series 8.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.719
Capaldi totally one-upped himself with the
bedroom.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.160
The kitchen was funny, but the bedroom was
better.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.359
Especially with him looking into Clara’s
vanity mirror.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:04.239
That’s a whole other conversation.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.860
What was he thinking about while waiting for
Clara to come back.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.970
I got a vibe from the first episode when he
was talking about the Robot forgetting who

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.980
he was.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:18.780
There were so many things in that Dinner Date,
Samuel Anderson turning on a dime, the way

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.670
he reacted to the war killings.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.790
I wonder where that’s going.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.090
And the wells.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:32.400
So I’ve been telling everyone to look at
the planets in the opening sequence and there’s

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.160
the one that looks like either Gallifrey or
Post-War Trenzalore but just in terms of quantity,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:42.920
there are about 27, which was the number of
planets Davros and the Daleks hid in the medusa

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:43.920
cascade.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:44.920
And Danny Pink dug 23 wells.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.970
I don’t think there’s any connection but
I did think about that for a moment.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:56.610
And when they paid the date off later, Clara
commented on the “Laws of Time”.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:02.320
I got the subtle dig at the classic doctor’s
being scolded by the Time Lords but I wonder.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.470
What are the actual Laws of Time?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:10.590
If you can remember a time they’ve ever
been directly referenced just write which

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.670
episode in the comments.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.170
Number 4 - Dan the Soldier Man

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.170
This was so trippy.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.310
Trying not to overthink it too much, but this
is where my mind went.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.771
Young Rupert is obsessed with the story he’s
created for his army figure, dan the soldier

00:02:23.771 --> 00:02:24.771
man.

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:29.310
Then, because of the courage Clara gives him
and the Doctor’s Fantasy Dream, he’s inceptioned

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.020
into joining the real life army one day so
that he can learn to be a hero.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.510
And to reaffirm that, he changes his name
to that of his childhood hero.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.569
Dan the soldier man.

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:42.090
Later the war takes it’s toll and we meet
him at coal hill school.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.100
But let’s think about what was said about
the story of Dan the Soldier man.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.390
He was destined to lead an army, but he didn’t
want to join said army.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.970
Missy is collecting souls or soldiers…

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:59.830
Real quick to finish this sentence I have
to talk about a quick finale spoiler so just

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:04.980
turn the volume down until this tag goes away...okay...here
we go..

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:10.440
What if Missy will create the army of cybermen
and try to force Danny to become the leader.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.420
And he’ll be the focal point of the doctor
stopping them.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.130
Just a new theory after listening to dan the
soldier man’s story.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.959
Okay, spoiler part over.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:22.390
Number 3 - Spaceman Danny Pink

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.950
Colonel Orson Pink from 100 years in the future.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:30.200
So many things here, I guess our children
will be pioneering time travel?

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.319
100 years isn’t that far away.

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:34.599
His whole story was just a self contained
thing.

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:38.630
I don’t think there was anything Sinister
about Orson but I do wonder if we’ll see

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:39.630
him again.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:43.260
It would be a fun twist on the Clara Impossible
Girl storyline to see multiple Danny Pink’s

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.260
coming and going.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.230
I totally believe that his time capsule malfunctioned
and sent him to the end of everything.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:50.510
The Robin Crusoe metaphor was perfect.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:55.230
And it implied that The Doctor will eventually
die a final death.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:01.260
At least unless he finds a way to exist in
the void outside of normal spacetime.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.200
That’s the crazy thing about trying to apply
logic to Doctor Who, there is always some

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.420
timey wimey workaround that will allow the
Doctor to walk away with a few scratches and

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.420
a new face.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.150
I don’t think we actually caught an exact
figure on the date of that final moment in

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.150
the universe.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.349
And for those wondering, Moffat wasn’t saying
the Universe was ending or time was ending.

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:23.010
Just that the universe had reached a point
in it’s expansion when all matter started

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:27.949
to drift apart.

00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:32.419
If you never watched, Neil Degrasse Tyson’s
Cosmos talks a lot about what is happening

00:04:32.419 --> 00:04:34.309
to the universe as time goes on.

00:04:34.309 --> 00:04:39.840
It’s expansion is accellerating, so eventually
all the galaxies and planets will just drift

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.139
apart until there’s no more gravity to hold
everything together.

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:45.990
That’s billions of years away though.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:53.219
Doctor Who Science Lession over, moving on.

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:56.479
Number 2 - The Shared Nightmare and new monster

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:00.870
I loved the idea of a universally shared experience
tied to a new type of monster.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:05.919
Yes, I do think the hiding creatures were
a new thing we haven’t seen before.

00:05:05.919 --> 00:05:08.610
If they had been the silence they would have
been way taller.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.490
And no, I don’t think moffat will ever show
us what they look like.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.729
He probably doesn’t even know what they
look like.

00:05:13.729 --> 00:05:17.729
The bedsheet is just meant to represent what
each of us pictures when we think of something

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:18.809
creeping under the bed.

00:05:18.809 --> 00:05:23.409
I got the sense that they were trying to make
a joke on the Doctor being the creature under

00:05:23.409 --> 00:05:24.409
the bed.

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:27.890
Like things go missing, strange noises, unexplained
things happen and it’s all because the doctor

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.439
is jumping around in time and space.

00:05:30.439 --> 00:05:33.710
It was a little creepy till they showed him
drinking the man’s coffee.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:35.919
Then I just understood it to be a joke.

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:38.479
I always forget how good the doctor is at
pinching stuff.

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:43.160
If he can pinch the Moment from the most secured
location on Gallifrey, he can pinch a cup

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.160
of coffee.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.232
Thematically, the idea of the Doctor as a
thief will continue in next week’s episode

00:05:46.232 --> 00:05:47.719
called “Time Heist”.

00:05:47.719 --> 00:05:51.589
and my Number 1 moment - A Stop over on Gallifrey

00:05:51.589 --> 00:05:56.009
I lost it a little when this happened, I thought
it was going to be some creepy barn Clara

00:05:56.009 --> 00:05:57.499
was forced to sleep in.

00:05:57.499 --> 00:06:02.089
In case you missed it, Clara’s speech at
the end explained that the Barn they were

00:06:02.089 --> 00:06:06.509
in was The Same Barn the John Hurt Doctor
took the Moment to in the 50th Anniversary.

00:06:06.509 --> 00:06:12.990
I know there was some confusion during the
50th about which planet he was on with all

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:13.999
the Sand.

00:06:13.999 --> 00:06:17.309
Everything I’ve read about this episode
says this barn scene was on Gallifrey.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:21.900
So Unless something weird was going on, John
Hurt was on Gallifrey during the 50th.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.900
I just love how they tie the idea of the Doctor’s
deepest fears to him committing his greatest

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.940
atrocity.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:36.009
Time isn’t really a circle, it’s more
like a river that forks, but Moffat, who actually

00:06:36.009 --> 00:06:41.539
did write this episode himself, gives us a
lot of information about the doctor’s motivation.

00:06:41.539 --> 00:06:46.830
He has, at all times since his first face,
been driven by fear.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.229
And thanks to the courage clara gave him,
he’s used that fear to become The Doctor.

00:06:51.229 --> 00:06:56.240
He wasn’t called the Doctor when he was
born, he gave himself that name.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.839
Probably as a result of what Clara told him.

00:06:58.839 --> 00:07:04.110
I try not to get too tied up in paradoxes
and timelines.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.499
But I love the thought that Clara is so fundamentally
tied to the Doctor’s life.

00:07:07.499 --> 00:07:08.499
All of his lives really.

00:07:08.499 --> 00:07:11.050
Like he wouldn’t be the Doctor if she had
never existed.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.151
It makes your head spin a little, because
you wonder how did things go down the first

00:07:14.151 --> 00:07:15.151
time.

00:07:15.151 --> 00:07:19.439
Because Clara didn’t exist before the doctor,
he presumably found her, then the impossible

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:23.529
girl storyline on trenzalore happened, cut
to millions of claras all over his timeline,

00:07:23.529 --> 00:07:28.819
cut to child doctor given the courage to join
the time lord academy by clara.

00:07:28.819 --> 00:07:29.919
Yikes.

00:07:29.919 --> 00:07:33.879
We’ll be talking about this plot point for
years.

00:07:33.879 --> 00:07:37.330
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was and where do you

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.279
think this episode ranks in terms of scary
doctor who episodes?

00:07:40.279 --> 00:07:43.789
I’d say it’s not the scariest, but I’d
put it in the top 20 at least.

00:07:43.789 --> 00:07:47.319
Here’s some of the bigger classic who and
other doctor references I noticed.

00:07:47.319 --> 00:07:49.999
Please add any you saw in the comments:

00:07:49.999 --> 00:07:51.869
First was the title of the episode, Listen.

00:07:51.869 --> 00:07:56.410
It reminds you a lot of the one word Doctor
Who episode titles and the fact it was a bit

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.699
horror made me think of Blink.

00:07:57.699 --> 00:07:59.870
Although I still think Blink is scarier.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.710
Then There’s Hide, that was Clara’s fourth
episode during series 7b.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.189
So a one word title fourth episode two series
in a row.

00:08:08.189 --> 00:08:12.969
We’ll have to see if the trend continues
next year during series 9.

00:08:12.969 --> 00:08:17.330
Everytime Clara and Danny Pink are together
the subject of Lady Killing comes up.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.599
That sounds like it’s going to be paid off
in the finale.

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:27.409
The Telepathic Link on the TARDIS is now my
favorite part of Capaldi’s TARDIS.

00:08:27.409 --> 00:08:30.969
It reminded me of something out of a frankenstein
story, especially with the steam punky look

00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:32.490
of the console and the rest of the room.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.490
The candles too.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:42.539
The new TARDIS is like a low-fi looking, sinister
looking frankenstein laboratory.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:47.490
This was the first time Capaldi has used the
Psychic Paper, glad to see that back.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:52.149
I remember when Matt Smith showed off an ID
badge once and it had a picture of the first

00:08:52.149 --> 00:08:53.880
doctor.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:09:04.640
The Toy Robot the doctor is handling here
in Danny’s room looks just like the Robot

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.149
from Tom Baker’s First Episode.

00:09:06.149 --> 00:09:10.430
Then the box of soldiers is just making me
hallucinate cybermen

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:18.660
And then when they’re at the end of everything
and the doctor is going on about silence,

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:23.519
it made me think of the Silence’s prophecy,
Silence will fall when the First Question

00:09:23.519 --> 00:09:24.519
is asked.

00:09:24.519 --> 00:09:25.519
Capaldi’s Doctor has been asking questions
non-stop.

00:09:25.519 --> 00:09:28.610
The creatures weren’t the silence, but it
makes me think that the silence’s prophecy

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.149
might carry forward into series 8 somehow.

00:09:31.149 --> 00:09:35.029
Overall I thought this episode was the strongest
of all the new ones so far.

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:37.209
I gave it a solid A plus.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:41.550
It didn’t linger too long on affectation
during the date scene and because Moffat has

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:45.180
that crazy Doctor Who mind palace and he wrote
the episode by himself.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:49.850
The story served as this huge bookend for
the Doctor’s Existence.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:54.959
Clara helped him become the doctor, so he
could one day go on to save clara and help

00:09:54.959 --> 00:09:56.790
her help himself become the doctor.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:00.560
I also love the way Danny Pink is becoming
a part of the team without even knowing it.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.210
His timeline is now fundamentally linked to
clara and the Doctors.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.870
This all feels like setup for a huge Danny
Pink moment in the finale.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.569
And the idea that Fear will take you home
feels so important now.

00:10:10.569 --> 00:10:14.860
Like the Doctor’s fear, missy’s fear,
clara’s fear and so on, will be the connective

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.769
tissue of series 8 in general.

00:10:16.769 --> 00:10:20.540
I read somewhere that there’s a lot of drama
going on behind the scenes on Doctor Who.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:25.790
With the producers and Moffat, and for whatever
reason, Moffat himself was dominating a lot

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.740
of the series 8 stories even though a bunch
of different writers worked on scripts.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.790
I don’t know if any of that is true, but
I definitely feel like episodes that are directly

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:35.060
connected to the big missy plot will benefit
from direct Moffat involvement.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.300
So with that in mind, here are the other episodes
Moffat is listed as writer on.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.269
There’s episode 5, Time Heist.

00:10:41.269 --> 00:10:42.569
That’s next week.

00:10:42.569 --> 00:10:47.620
Episode 6, The Caretaker, in two weeks and
the final two epsiodes 11 and 12.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.790
That’s Dark Water and Death in Heaven respectively.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.639
So I’d expect that those episodes will directly
tie in with the Missy plot.

00:10:54.639 --> 00:10:58.889
Just in terms of the acting, Capaldi was fantastic
all by himself.

00:10:58.889 --> 00:11:14.940
I love watching him lecture himself and Samuel
Anderson did an amazing job of creating a

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:28.029
future Danny Pink, even though technically
it was his grandson.

00:11:28.029 --> 00:11:33.029
My next video will be my top 5 scary episodes
of Doctor Who.

00:11:33.029 --> 00:11:34.029
I’ll post that tonight.

00:11:34.029 --> 00:11:35.029
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:11:35.029 --> 00:11:37.139
And my Q&amp;A will post on Sunday.

00:11:37.139 --> 00:11:41.779
So leave all your questions about the stopover
on gallifrey, the missy plot and anything

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:42.779
else you want me to include.

00:11:42.779 --> 00:11:46.380
I’ll announce the giveaway winner when I
post the Q&amp;A.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:50.440
Right now click here for the bonus video and
click here for the Q&amp;A.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.640
I’ll update the annotations as soon as soon
as I post them.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:53.640
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:53.642
High Fives!

